Lab 19: Using ipa-client-install for RHEL Enrollment
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Understand the purpose and benefits of enrolling RHEL clients into an Identity Management (IdM) domain
Successfully enroll RHEL client systems into an existing IdM domain using the ipa-client-install command
Test client authentication using Kerberos authentication with the kinit command
Configure and verify SSSD (System Security Services Daemon) for seamless Kerberos authentication
Troubleshoot common enrollment issues and verify proper client configuration
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command-line operations
Familiarity with Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL) system administration
Knowledge of basic networking concepts (DNS, hostnames, IP addresses)
Understanding of authentication concepts (usernames, passwords, Kerberos basics)
Access to a functioning IdM server environment
Administrative privileges on the client system you'll be enrolling
